1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:09,021
High in the Ethiopian mountains at dawn,
an ancient wisdom awakens with the mist.

2
00:00:09,271 --> 00:00:19,392
Elder weaver Ato Bekele works his loom,
speaking softly to young Selam.

3
00:00:19,642 --> 00:00:27,392
Look at this single cotton thread—
alone, even a gentle breeze snaps it.

4
00:00:27,642 --> 00:00:35,392
Selam holds the thread and listens,
wondering how fragility becomes strength.

5
00:00:35,642 --> 00:00:43,892
As fresh jebena coffee fills the home,
neighbors gather together as custom calls.

6
00:00:44,142 --> 00:00:52,392
In the village courtyard, many hands
turn heavy stones into shared ease.

7
00:00:52,642 --> 00:01:00,892
As our ancestors taught from long ago:
When spiderwebs unite, they tie a lion.

8
00:01:01,142 --> 00:01:10,103
When fine threads weave with patience,
they form unbreakable cloth and community.

9
00:01:10,353 --> 00:01:18,834
Wherever we stand in the world today,
our unity turns small acts into strength.
